<title>UK: LME copper nudges higher in late trading.</title>
<headline>LME copper nudges higher in late trading.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>LME copper was barely firmer in late inter-office trading on Thursday evening.</p>
<p>At 1800 GMT, three months was indicated at $2,364/67, up a touch from it $2,360 kerb close.</p>
<p>After the weak kerb close, prices were expected to consolidate in thin activity on Friday ahead of the three-day weekend in Britain.</p>
<p>Nearby support was pegged at $2,350 with first resistance at $2,380.</p>
<p>Scant movement was seen in the other metals.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542-8065</p>
